@@ -0,0 +1,38 @@
+Feature: Routing
+  As a user
+  I want to filter my todos by their completion state
+  So that I can focus on active or completed tasks
+
+  Background:
+    Given the app is loaded
+    And I have added todos titled "Active task" and "Completed task"
+    And "Completed task" is completed
+
+  Scenario: Default route shows all todos
+    Given the URL hash is "#/"
+    Then I see a todo with the title "Active task"
+    And I see a todo with the title "Completed task"
+
+  Scenario: Active filter shows only active todos
+    When I click the "Active" filter link
+    Then I see a todo with the title "Active task"
+    And I do not see a todo with the title "Completed task"
+    And the "Active" filter link has the selected class
+
+  Scenario: Completed filter shows only completed todos
+    When I click the "Completed" filter link
+    Then I see a todo with the title "Completed task"
+    And I do not see a todo with the title "Active task"
+    And the "Completed" filter link has the selected class
+
+  Scenario: All filter shows all todos
+    Given I am viewing the active filter
+    When I click the "All" filter link
+    Then I see a todo with the title "Active task"
+    And I see a todo with the title "Completed task"
+    And the "All" filter link has the selected class
+
+  Scenario: Completing a todo hides it in active filter
+    Given I am viewing the active filter
+    When I toggle the todo "Active task" as completed
+    Then I do not see a todo with the title "Active task"
