@@ -0,0 +1,46 @@
+Feature: Todo Editing
+  As a user
+  I want to edit my todo titles
+  So that I can correct mistakes or update tasks
+
+  Background:
+    Given the app is loaded
+    And I have added a todo titled "Original title"
+
+  Scenario: Double-clicking a todo label activates editing mode
+    When I double-click the label of todo "Original title"
+    Then the todo item has the editing class
+    And the edit input is focused and contains "Original title"
+
+  Scenario: Saving an edit on Enter key
+    When I double-click the label of todo "Original title"
+    And I change the edit input value to "Updated title"
+    And I press Enter in the edit input
+    Then the todo item no longer has the editing class
+    And the todo label shows "Updated title"
+
+  Scenario: Saving an edit on blur
+    When I double-click the label of todo "Original title"
+    And I change the edit input value to "Updated title"
+    And the edit input loses focus
+    Then the todo item no longer has the editing class
+    And the todo label shows "Updated title"
+
+  Scenario: Empty edit destroys the todo
+    When I double-click the label of todo "Original title"
+    And I change the edit input value to ""
+    And I press Enter in the edit input
+    Then I do not see a todo with the title "Original title"
+
+  Scenario: Whitespace-only edit destroys the todo
+    When I double-click the label of todo "Original title"
+    And I change the edit input value to "   "
+    And I press Enter in the edit input
+    Then I do not see a todo with the title "Original title"
+
+  Scenario: Escape key cancels editing and restores original title
+    When I double-click the label of todo "Original title"
+    And I change the edit input value to "Changed title"
+    And I press Escape in the edit input
+    Then the todo item no longer has the editing class
+    And the todo label shows "Original title"
